{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Stand still and see the salvation of YHWH.</b> For you shall not wage war, but only see the salvation of YHWH that He will do for you today. One may wonder: how could a great camp of six hundred thousand men fear those pursuing them, and why would they not fight for their lives, for their children? The answer: because the Egyptians were masters over Israel, and this generation that came out of Egypt learned from youth to bear the Egyptian yoke, and its spirit was low. How could it now fight its masters? Israel were feeble and untrained for war. Behold, Amalek came with a small people — were it not for the prayer of Moses, he would have weakened Israel. And HaShem alone, who does great things (Job 5:9), and for whom plots are formed (I Samuel 20:3), brought it about that all the males who came out of Egypt died, for they had no strength to fight the Canaanites, until another generation arose, the wilderness generation, who had not seen exile and possessed a high spirit, as I have mentioned in my words on Moses in the section \"And these are the names.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:26.071390011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}